.\" mutar.1 — man page for µtar (mutar)
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH MUTAR 1 "2026-08-16" "mutar 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mutar \- µtar GNU-tar-compatible archiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mutar
.RI [ OPTION... ]
.RI [ FILE... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mutar
(brand name
.BR µtar )
is a ground-up C++23 reimplementation of GNU tar.
It is
.B not
Jörg Schilling's
.B star
(Schily tools).
.PP
Compatibility goal is approximately
.B 99%
with GNU tar 1.35 for common archive formats
.RB ( v7 ,
.BR oldgnu ,
.BR gnu ,
.BR ustar ,
.BR pax / posix )
and the command-line interface described in
.BR tar (1).
.B SELinux is not supported
(no test hardware; options are accepted as no-ops with a warning).
.PP
In addition to GNU tar-compatible operations, mutar provides an optional
sidecar member index and seek-friendly compression for faster selective
list/extract on large archives.
.SH OPTIONS
This section summarizes main operations and mutar-specific options.
For the full GNU-compatible option set, run
.B mutar \-\-help
or see
.BR tar (1).
.SS Main operations
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create
Create a new archive.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extract ", " \-\-get
Extract files from an archive.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-list
List archive contents.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-append
Append files to the end of an archive.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Append only files newer than the archive copy.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-catenate ", " \-\-concatenate
Append tar archives to an archive.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff ", " \-\-compare
Find differences between archive and filesystem.
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Delete members from an archive (seekable, uncompressed).
.TP
.B \-\-test\-label
Test or print the archive volume label.
.SS Common options
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file=\fIARCHIVE\fR
Use archive file or device
.IR ARCHIVE
(use
.B \-
for stdin/stdout).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
List files processed.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-gzip
Filter through gzip.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-bzip2
Filter through bzip2.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-xz
Filter through xz.
.TP
.B \-\-zstd
Filter through zstd.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-directory=\fIDIR\fR
Change to directory
.I DIR
before performing operations.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-absolute\-names
Do not strip leading
.B /
from member names (disabled under
.BR \-\-restrict ).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-preserve\-permissions
Extract file permissions.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sparse
Handle sparse files efficiently.
.TP
.BI \-H " FORMAT" "\fR, \fB\-\-format=" FORMAT
Create archive in
.I FORMAT
.RB ( v7 ,
.BR oldgnu ,
.BR gnu ,
.BR ustar ,
.BR pax ).
Default write format is
.BR gnu .
.SS Mutar-specific options
.TP
.B \-\-write\-index
On create, write a sidecar member index next to the archive as
.IR ARCHIVE .mutaridx
(format
.BR MUTAR.INDEX.V1 ).
Enables fast selective list/extract when the index is present.
.TP
.BI \-\-mutar\-index= FILE
Use
.I FILE
as the sidecar index path (write on create; read on list/extract).
.TP
.B \-\-seekable
Prefer seek-friendly compression for xz (multi-block) and zstd (chunked).
Implies index generation.
On compressed extract with an index, mutar materializes a temporary
uncompressed view once, then seeks via the index (not true frame-level
seek without materialize).
.SS PAX and multi-volume notes
.TP
.BI \-\-pax\-option= delete= KEYWORD [,...]
When writing PAX archives, suppress the listed keywords
.RB ( delete=
only; other
.B \-\-pax\-option
keywords are currently ignored).
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-multi\-volume
Create, list, or extract multi-volume archives.
.TP
.BI \-L " N" "\fR, \fB\-\-tape\-length=" N
Rotate volume after approximately
.IR N "×1024"
bytes (implies
.BR \-M ).
Rotation is
.B between members
only; mid-file split across volumes is not supported.
.TP
.BI \-F " SCRIPT" "\fR, \fB\-\-info\-script=" SCRIPT
Run
.I SCRIPT
at each volume boundary (implies
.BR \-M ).
Environment includes
.B TAR_ARCHIVE
and
.BR TAR_VOLUME ;
non-zero exit fails the operation.
.TP
.BI \-\-volno\-file= F
Read/write the current volume number in file
.I F
(atomic update).
.SS Security-related options
.TP
.B \-\-restrict
Forbid
.BR \-P / \-\-absolute\-names ,
.BR \-\-to\-command ,
and multi-volume mode.
.TP
Path sanitization on extract strips leading
.B /
(unless
.BR \-P )
and collapses
.B ..
components so members cannot escape the destination directory.
.SH DIFFERENCES FROM GNU TAR
.IP \(bu 3
Product identity is
.B µtar
/
.BR mutar ,
not GNU tar and not Schily
.BR star .
.IP \(bu 3
SELinux
.RB ( \-\-selinux ,
.BR \-\-no\-selinux )
is unsupported: options are accepted as no-ops with a warning.
.IP \(bu 3
Sidecar index
.RB ( \-\-write\-index ,
.BR \-\-mutar\-index )
and
.B \-\-seekable
are mutar extensions.
.IP \(bu 3
.B \-\-pax\-option
implements
.B delete=KEYWORD
only.
.IP \(bu 3
Multi-volume supports between-member create/extract and volume scripts;
mid-file continuation is not implemented.
.IP \(bu 3
Remote tape
.RB ( rmt )
supports open/read/write/close; remote lseek and remote append are not
implemented.
.IP \(bu 3
Listed-incremental
.RB ( \-g )
snapshot V2 records files and directories with mtime and device; the skip
filter is regular-file only (directories are always dumped).
.IP \(bu 3
.B \-\-sparse\-version
is accepted but write always emits sparse format 1.0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ARCHIVE.mutaridx
Default sidecar index path when
.B \-\-write\-index
is used without
.BR \-\-mutar\-index .
Binary format magic
.BR MUTAR.INDEX.V1 :
per-member name, header offset, and size for seek extract.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B non\-zero
Usage error, I/O failure, verification failure, or subprocess error
(depending on options such as
.BR \-\-ignore\-failed\-read ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Create a gzip-compressed archive
mutar \-czf project.tar.gz src/

# Extract into a directory
mutar \-xf archive.tar \-C /tmp/dest

# Create with sidecar index
mutar \-cf archive.tar \-\-write\-index tree/

# Seek-friendly xz + index
mutar \-cJf archive.tar.xz \-\-seekable tree/

# List using an explicit index
mutar \-tf archive.tar \-\-mutar\-index=archive.mutaridx
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tar (1),
.BR gzip (1),
.BR bzip2 (1),
.BR xz (1),
.BR zstd (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
.IR README.md ,
